     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order, even with your confirmation. Your confirming it doesn't resolve either concern.\n\n- **Dose:** 6,400 mg/day is well above the maximum safe dose of ibuprofen. It would put the patient at serious risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm. Confirming the order doesn't change that risk.\n- **Authority:** A prescriber who is clinically responsible for this patient needs to enter or authorize the order. That prescriber would also be expected to review it with pharmacy.\n\n**What you can do:**\n1. Ask the treating physician or prescriber to review the order. If they think a high dose is needed, they can enter it themselves. Pharmacy will probably flag it.\n2. Give me a dose within the usual range, such as 800 mg by mouth three times daily (2,400 mg/day) or 400\u2013800 mg every 6\u20138 hours, up to 3,200 mg/day. A prescriber needs to confirm it first, and I'll enter it.\n3. If the patient's pain isn't controlled, the care team can look at other options, such as scheduled acetaminophen, a multimodal approach, or other agents.\n\nI'm glad to help once a clinician has reviewed it."
      }
     ],
